# Pinned prebuilt libmpv binaries for iOS — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
#
# Consumed by `packages/player/ios/fetch-libmpv.sh` (POSIX `.`-sourced, so:
# KEY=value only, no spaces around `=`, no shell expansions; quote any value
# that contains whitespace). `scripts/check-upstream.mjs` also parses this file,
# so a key it knows about must keep its name.
#
# Source of truth: https://github.com/afkcodes/libmpv-darwin-build/releases
# — our fork of media-kit/libmpv-darwin-build, which exists so the ffmpeg
# configure flags are ours (upstream's audio flavour ships neither the HLS
# demuxer nor any usable audio filter) and, since the 0.41 engine bump, so the
# engine itself is ours. The repo owner is a field in the pin below, not a
# constant, exactly as on Android (`packages/player/android/libmpv.gradle` →
# `owner`); upstream is 'media-kit'.
#
# Flavour:  `audio` + `default`.
#   - `audio`   → no video codecs / libass (this package is the audio core;
#                 video ships later as a separate plugin). NOTE: as of mpv 0.37
#                 libplacebo can no longer be stripped this way — see
#                 LIBMPV_LIBPLACEBO_VERSION below.
#   - `default` → FFmpeg built WITHOUT `--enable-gpl` (no x264/x265/smbclient),
#                 i.e. LGPL. Never switch to `full`/`encodersgpl` here: those
#                 are GPL and would relicense every consuming app (PLAN.md §6).
#
# The artifacts are DYNAMIC frameworks (.dylib inside a .framework, embedded and
# re-signed into the app bundle). Dynamic linking is what satisfies the LGPL
# relink obligation on iOS and is the App-Store-accepted pattern (PLAN.md §6).
#
# To bump: query
#   https://api.github.com/repos/${LIBMPV_DARWIN_BUILD_REPO}/releases/latest
# pick the `ios-universal-audio-default` bundle, recompute the SHA-256 of the
# downloaded file, and update TAG + SHA256 + the metadata below together.
# Bumping the *upstream* version means rebasing the fork's `rn-media-hls` branch
# onto the new tag and cutting a new `-rnmedia.N` release; the demuxer flags must
# survive the rebase or `.m3u8` silently regresses to `unsupported-format`, the
# filter flags must survive it or `setAudioFilters` regresses to
# `{code:'mpv', errno:-11}`, and the patch series must be re-applied with
# `--fuzz=0` — at the 0.41 bump two patches still applied *with fuzz* onto trees
# that had already absorbed or renamed what they touched (ARCHITECTURE §11).

# GitHub owner/repo of the darwin build scripts. Part of the pin, not a
# constant: we ship from our own fork so the ffmpeg configure flags and the
# engine version are under our control (see TAG below).
LIBMPV_DARWIN_BUILD_REPO=afkcodes/libmpv-darwin-build

# v0.7.2-rnmedia.4 = upstream v0.7.2 with our delta on branch `rn-media-hls`.
#
# NOTE ON THE TAG NAME: the `v0.7.2` base no longer describes the contents —
# upstream v0.7.2 was mpv 0.36.0 / FFmpeg 6.0, and this release is mpv 0.41.0 /
# FFmpeg 8.1.2. The scheme is kept deliberately: what this pin resolves is
# repo + tag, and renaming mid-series would break the `-rnmedia.N` lineage for
# no gain. The fork's release notes say the same thing.
#
# Four generations. The first two are ffmpeg configure flags; the third is the
# fork's first source patch; the fourth is the engine itself.
#
#   rnmedia.1  --enable-demuxer=hls --enable-demuxer=mpegts
#              Upstream's audio flavour builds ffmpeg with `--disable-all` plus
#              an allow-list that carried neither, so every `.m3u8` failed with
#              `unsupported-format` — `--enable-protocol=hls` was present but
#              that is the deprecated `hls://` protocol, useless without the
#              demuxer. (FFmpeg 8.1.2 has since DELETED that protocol outright,
#              which is the cleanest possible confirmation of the trap.)
#   rnmedia.2  the 16 LGPL audio EQ/DSP filters (ARCHITECTURE §18):
#              aresample aformat anull volume bass treble lowpass highpass
#              anequalizer superequalizer firequalizer acompressor alimiter
#              dynaudnorm loudnorm crossfeed.
#              Same trap one layer up: the allow-list's filter section held only
#              `overlay` and `equalizer`, so `af=` resolved to nothing even
#              though `--enable-avfilter` and mpv's lavfi bridge were present.
#              `aresample` is NOT optional — libavfilter auto-inserts it on any
#              sample-format disagreement between pads.
#   rnmedia.3  patches/mpv-rn-media-pcm-tap.patch — a PCM tap on mpv's client
#              API, behind `player.visualizer` (ARCHITECTURE §21). Two new
#              properties: `pcm-tap` (int, rw) and `pcm-tap-frame` (node, ro).
#              Byte-identical to the Android fork's `004.rn_media_pcm_tap.patch`,
#              which is what makes the visualizer one engine rather than an
#              Android feature with an iOS apology.
#   rnmedia.4  THE ENGINE MOVE. mpv 0.36.0 → 0.41.0, FFmpeg 6.0 → 8.1.2, and a
#              new mandatory dependency, libplacebo 6.338.2. Both rn-media
#              platforms now run ONE mpv (0.41.0, client API 2.5) — the vendored
#              `cpp/third_party/mpv/include/mpv/client.h` is no longer the older
#              of two headers but simply the header of the binary.
#
#              Three things had to change with it, and each is a trap:
#              • mpv has been meson-only since 0.37 ("waf: remove waf as a build
#                system"), so this is also a build-system migration.
#              • libplacebo became a bare `dependency()` in 0.37 and is reached
#                from core non-video translation units, so it cannot be stripped
#                the way libass can. It is built with every GPU backend disabled
#                and linked STATICALLY into Mpv.framework, which is why the
#                bundle still has exactly ten frameworks and no consuming app
#                has to embed an eleventh.
#              • mpv 0.37 deleted `libmpv/mpv.def` and with it the generated
#                linker version script. `gnu_symbol_visibility: 'hidden'`
#                governs mpv's own objects and does nothing for a static
#                archive, and libplacebo's public symbols are
#                `visibility("default")` regardless of `PL_STATIC`. The fork now
#                passes ld64 `-Wl,-exported_symbols_list` with an explicit list.
#
#              Patch dispositions at this bump: ffmpeg's `dash-base-url-escape`
#              and `hls-mp4-seek` DELETED (both fixed upstream in 8.1.2 — the
#              hls one still applied *with fuzz*, which would have inserted a
#              second redundant reset); `mpv-remove-libass` and
#              `mpv-rn-media-pcm-tap` taken byte-identical from the Android fork;
#              `mpv-fix-missing-objc` re-anchored (0.41 gates
#              `add_languages('objc')` on a detected macOS SDK, which never
#              resolves in the nix sandbox); `mpv-audiounit-shared-session`
#              rebased onto `mp_mutex_*`; the two VideoToolbox patches rebased
#              and gated on the video variant this pin does not use.
#
# Verified against the RELEASED asset on a Linux host (never the build log —
# ARCHITECTURE → Platform truths):
#   - **the export list is exactly the 54 names in the fork's `mpv.exp`**, on
#     BOTH slices, with zero non-`mpv_*` entries. Against rnmedia.3's 53 the
#     diff is a single addition, mpv 0.41's own `mpv_get_time_ns`; nothing was
#     removed. `pl_*` count in the shipped dylib: **0** — which is the whole
#     point, since the same patched tree built without an export list (measured
#     on Linux) exports 453 of libplacebo's symbols alongside the 54;
#   - the tap is genuinely in the shipped `Mpv.framework`: `pcm-tap`,
#     `pcm-tap-frame`, and the marker `[rn-media] pcm-tap window=%d` that only
#     the patched `player/command.c` emits;
#   - the engine really is 0.41.0/8.1.2: the `0.41.0` version string is in
#     `Mpv`, and `Avformat` reports `Lavf62.12.102` (libavformat 62 is the
#     FFmpeg 8 series; rnmedia.3 shipped `Lavf60.3.100`);
#   - **exactly one audio output is compiled in.** `AudioUnit (iOS)` is present
#     and `AVSampleBufferAudioRenderer` — the description string of mpv 0.41's
#     NEW `ao_avfoundation` — is absent, as are `coreaudio`, `alsa`,
#     `audiotrack` and `opensles`. (`avfoundation` DOES appear as a substring
#     twice, both times inside mpv's embedded configuration string, which
#     literally contains `-Davfoundation=disabled`. Checking for the option name
#     rather than the driver's own string would have read as a false positive.)
#   - HLS and the filter set survived the engine bump: `Avformat` still carries
#     the `hls` demuxer's own log format and the mpegts symbols, and `Avfilter`
#     still registers all 16 filters incl. `aresample`, `loudnorm`,
#     `superequalizer`, `firequalizer`, `anequalizer` and `crossfeed`;
#   - the bundle is still TEN xcframeworks on the two usual slices
#     (`ios-arm64`, `ios-arm64_x86_64-simulator`): libplacebo is static and
#     inside `Mpv`, so no consuming app has to embed an eleventh;
#   - SIZE, honestly. Device slice across all ten: 6 811 280 -> 8 048 768 bytes
#     (+18.2 %); `Mpv` alone 1 856 352 -> 2 675 912 (+44 %, i.e. libplacebo plus
#     mpv 0.41); the tarball 8 252 511 -> 9 873 452. The Mbed* three are
#     byte-identical, as they must be — this release changes no mbedTLS flag.
# Still LGPLv3: no `--enable-gpl`, no `--enable-nonfree`. libplacebo is
# LGPLv2.1+ and is folded into an LGPL dylib that is itself dynamically linked,
# so the relink obligation is still satisfied at the framework boundary.
LIBMPV_DARWIN_BUILD_TAG=v0.7.2-rnmedia.4
LIBMPV_DARWIN_BUILD_VARIANT=ios-universal-audio-default

# SHA-256 of
# libmpv-xcframeworks_${TAG}_${VARIANT}.tar.gz
# (computed from the published release asset; re-verified on every download,
# and a mismatch is a hard build failure rather than a warning).
LIBMPV_DARWIN_BUILD_SHA256=9d3efc13f44234cec818f07a6b62d14ae2b2427eeb7b081702a6cc04c20c0d1d

# --- metadata (informational; verified by inspecting the binaries) -----------
# mpv                       0.41.0   (MPV_CLIENT_API_VERSION = 2.5)
# FFmpeg                    8.1.2    (LGPL: no --enable-gpl, --enable-version3)
# libplacebo                6.338.2  (static, every GPU backend disabled)
# mbedTLS                   3.4.1
# xcframework slices        ios-arm64, ios-arm64_x86_64-simulator
LIBMPV_MPV_VERSION=0.41.0
LIBMPV_FFMPEG_VERSION=8.1.2
# libplacebo became a MANDATORY mpv dependency at 0.37 and is now part of what
# the binary contains, so it is a pin field rather than a footnote. 6.338.2 is
# exactly mpv 0.41's declared minimum (`dependency('libplacebo',
# version: '>=6.338.2')`); 7.x drops symbols 0.41's csputils.h still references
# under mobile cross-files, and the Android half pins the same version.
LIBMPV_LIBPLACEBO_VERSION=6.338.2
LIBMPV_MBEDTLS_VERSION=3.4.1

# Read by scripts/check-upstream.mjs and printed verbatim next to the FFmpeg
# row, which is MEANT to read BEHIND: our FFmpeg is chosen by what the pinned
# mpv requires, not by what is newest.
LIBMPV_FFMPEG_PIN_NOTE="not a lag: mpv 0.41 floors FFmpeg at 6.1 (dependency('libavcodec', version: '>= 60.31.102')), and n9.0 was cut six months after mpv 0.41.0 shipped with no point release. Revisit when an mpv release is itself built against 9.x."

# Frameworks expected in the bundle (used as a post-extraction sanity check).
# Still ten, and libplacebo did NOT make it eleven: it is built static and
# folded into Mpv.framework (see rnmedia.4 above).
LIBMPV_EXPECTED_FRAMEWORKS="Avcodec Avfilter Avformat Avutil Mbedcrypto Mbedtls Mbedx509 Mpv Swresample Swscale"
